1
00:00:04,370 --> 00:00:06,640
什么味 你是在用大锅洗衣服吗
Ew. Are you doing laundry on the stove

2
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:07,620
就像古代那样
like in olden times?

3
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:08,800
我的天 咱家没钱了吗
Oh, my God. Are we poor?

4
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:10,700
我就知道老爸的魔术用品店会毁了我们
I knew Dad's magic shop would destroy us.

5
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:13,598
不 是我贝奇姑姑最喜欢的番茄汤
No, it is my Aunt Becky's favorite tomato soup,

6
00:00:13,598 --> 00:00:14,580
我要带去给她
and I am bringing it to her

7
00:00:14,580 --> 00:00:16,080
因为她中风了正在养病
because she's recovering from a stroke.

8
00:00:16,220 --> 00:00:18,660
她是你们过去很怕的那个刻薄姑姑吗
Is she the mean one you guys used to be so scared of?

9
00:00:18,740 --> 00:00:20,560
老天 是的 特别是你米奇尔舅舅
Oh, God, yes, especially Uncle Mitchell.

10
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:22,020
就像他是一头虚弱的瞪羚
It was like he was a weak gazelle

11
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:23,860
而她是一头饥饿又恐同的猎豹
and she was a hungry, homophobic cheetah.

12
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:25,997
无意冒犯 但那汤太难闻了
No offense, but that soup stinks.

13
00:00:25,997 --> 00:00:27,800
哪有 挺好闻的
No, it smells fine.

14
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:29,460
有人在烧飞盘吗
Is someone burning Frisbees?

15
00:00:29,460 --> 00:00:30,620
是汤
It's soup!

16
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:32,200
不 这可不是汤味
No, that's not it.

17
00:00:32,940 --> 00:00:34,620
瞧瞧你穿得这么正式
Oh, look at you all dressed up.

18
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:36,540
跟我们一起去看米奇尔舅舅冒冷汗吗
Coming with us to watch Uncle Mitchell sweat?

19
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:38,540
不 阿尔文的爸爸从伦敦来了
No, Arvin's dad is in from London,

20
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:39,620
他想让我见见他
and he wants me to meet him.

21
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:41,020
等等
Hang on.

22
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:42,480
你没有宿醉
You're not hungover.

23
00:00:43,280 --> 00:00:45,140
发型很保守 没露乳沟
Hair's conservative, no cleavage.

24
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:47,000
我的天 你想留个好印象
Oh, my God. You're trying to make a good impression.

25
00:00:47,140 --> 00:00:47,900
你爱上他了
You're in love!

26
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:48,970
住口 我没有
Shut up. I am not.

27
00:00:48,970 --> 00:00:50,400
我可说不准
Ohh, I don't know.

28
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:51,860
我看到你这次谈恋爱有多用心了
I see how hard you work at this relationship.

29
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:53,620
你起早去看足球赛
You woke up early to watch soccer

30
00:00:53,620 --> 00:00:54,800
用的还是英式叫法
and you called it football.

31
00:00:54,960 --> 00:00:56,280
冷静点
Oh, just calm down.

32
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:57,480
这才三个月
It's been three months,

33
00:00:57,480 --> 00:00:59,840
而且人人都知道今年利物浦队特别顺
and everyone knows Liverpool is having a cracking good year.

34
00:01:00,180 --> 00:01:02,920
尽管如此 见家长仍是恋爱一大里程碑
Still, meeting a parent is a major relationship milestone.

35
00:01:03,220 --> 00:01:04,300
克莱尔 你让我有所期望了
Claire, you're getting my hopes up,

36
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:05,700
安迪留下的旧伤我还没疗好呢
and I still haven't recovered from Andy.

37
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,320
更别提迪兰了
And don't even get me started on Dylan.

38
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:10,160
我每次看到睡在车里的人都会忍不住怀念旧时
I get nostalgic every time I see someone sleeping in their car.

39
00:01:11,580 --> 00:01:12,820
-你紧张吗 -不紧张
- You nervous? - No.

40
00:01:12,820 --> 00:01:14,460
就算我紧张 我也早有准备
And even if I were, I've got it covered.

41
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:16,400
我从诺普带回了这些新贴纸
I've got these new stickers from NERP.

42
00:01:17,380 --> 00:01:19,480
我们的最新产品
So, our latest product

43
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:21,940
是最惊人的科技大突破
is the most amazing scientific breakthrough --

44
00:01:23,940 --> 00:01:24,380
贴纸
stickers!

45
00:01:24,540 --> 00:01:25,420
你真是个天才
Oh, you're a genius.

46
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:27,360
我们生活的时代太棒了 我承受不住了
What an amazing time we live in. I can't.

47
00:01:27,540 --> 00:01:29,360
这些贴纸能减压
So, they're designed to reduce stress

48
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:31,760
助你大胆地去追求辉煌
and to help you boldly pursue greatness

49
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:34,080
它能扰乱你大脑中理性的部分
by scrambling the rational part of the brain

50
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:36,580
让你不再自问"这样真的好吗"
that asks, "Does this seem right?"

51
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:41,680
总之 因为我不能用小白鼠做实验
Anyway, since I can't test on laboratory rats,

52
00:01:41,720 --> 00:01:43,760
我需要你们来试用
I'm gonna need you guys to try them.

53
00:01:44,120 --> 00:01:45,280
-好的 -好的
- Okay. - Okay.

54
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:47,500
等等 这里没人有起搏器
So, wait -- No one here has a pacemaker

55
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:49,140
或做律师的父母 对吗
or lawyer parents, right?

56
00:01:49,631 --> 00:01:51,001
-没有 -没有
- No. - ?No.

57
00:01:51,160 --> 00:01:52,860
那快试用起来吧
Then test away!

58
00:02:06,420 --> 00:02:08,140
我去问问贝奇在哪间病房
I'll go see what room Becky's in,

59
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:10,480
或者我们可以摸摸哪个门把手阴气逼人
or we can just feel for which doorknob is cold.

60
00:02:10,520 --> 00:02:12,457
菲尔 菲尔 你看到街对面有什么了吗
Phil, Phil. Did you see what's across the street?

61
00:02:12,457 --> 00:02:14,260
-密室逃脱 -我看到了
- An escape room. - Oh, I did.

62
00:02:14,260 --> 00:02:15,100
不 不去
No, we're not doing that.

63
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:16,020
绝对不去
No way in hell.

64
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:17,760
她连冰淇淋都要拒绝
She also said no to ice cream.

65
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:19,260
密室逃脱 那是什么
Escape room? What is that?

66
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:21,340
是个主题房间 他们把你锁在里面
Oh, it's a themed room that they lock you in,

67
00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:22,960
然后你必须解开谜题和线索
and then you have to solve puzzles and clues

68
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:24,660
才能逃脱
to, um, you know, escape.

69
00:02:24,780 --> 00:02:26,300
否则会被他们割掉手指吗
Or they cut off your finger?

70
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:28,120
什么 不
What? No.

71
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:29,720
-只是玩个好玩 -是的
- It's just for fun. - Yeah.

72
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:31,480
可那就没有高风险的刺激感了
Oh, but then that lowers the stakes.

73
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:34,380
好了 她在208号房 我们走
Okay. She's in Room 208. Let's go.

74
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:36,000
杰 你听到了吗
Jay, did you hear that

75
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:38,160
街对面有密室逃脱
there is an escape room across the street?

76
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:39,280
-我们不去 -为什么
- We're not doing that. - Why not?

77
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:41,340
因为你在高压情境下
Because when you get in a stressful situation,

78
00:02:41,340 --> 00:02:42,340
就会开始大吼
you start to scream,

79
00:02:42,340 --> 00:02:44,580
我可不想在上锁房间里体验那些
and I'm not taking that show into a locked room.

80
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:46,700
是的 这家伙连堵车超过五分钟
Yeah, and this one gets panicked if he's stuck in traffic

81
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:47,728
都会恐慌
for more than five minutes.

82
00:02:47,728 --> 00:02:48,980
看来就咱俩去了
Guess it's just you and me.

83
00:02:48,980 --> 00:02:50,020
绝对不去 亲爱的
Oh, hard pass, honey.

84
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:51,180
在密闭空间里
In a confined space,

85
00:02:51,180 --> 00:02:52,700
你会像《飞天法宝》一样过度亢奋
you're just bouncing off the wall like Flubber.

86
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:56,640
大家都知道我和我妹妹贝奇不合
It's no secret my sister Becky and I have our differences.

87
00:02:56,650 --> 00:02:58,340
他们九年没说过话了
They haven't talked in nine years.

88
00:02:58,340 --> 00:02:59,340
她就像怪物一样
She's kind of a monster.

89
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:01,800
我只在我们的婚礼上见过她一次
I've only met her once, at our wedding.

90
00:03:02,180 --> 00:03:05,660
想象一下 把杰身上所有最糟糕的缺点
Imagine if you took all of Jay's worst qualities

91
00:03:05,660 --> 00:03:07,020
都塞进一套女士裤装里
and wrapped them in a pantsuit.

92
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:08,680
可我一听说她中风了
But as soon as I heard she had a stroke,

93
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:10,120
我知道我必须赶去她身边
I knew I had to rush to her side.

94
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:11,560
那是三周前的事
It happened three weeks ago.

95
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:13,660
在冰球季后赛进行到一半的时候中风
Right in the middle of hockey playoffs!

96
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:14,980
典型的贝奇扰人作风
Typical Becky!

97
00:03:17,080 --> 00:03:18,580
她在那
Okay. There she is.

98
00:03:19,140 --> 00:03:20,080
贝奇姑姑
Hi, Aunt Becky.

99
00:03:20,720 --> 00:03:21,638
她好像睡着了
I think she's sleeping.

100
00:03:21,638 --> 00:03:24,180
那副讨人厌嘴脸连睡着时都还在
With the same mean old puss on her face.

101
00:03:24,180 --> 00:03:25,760
米奇尔 你为什么不去亲她一下
Hey, Mitchell. Why don't you give her a little kiss?

102
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:26,721
你去亲她
You give her a little kiss.

103
00:03:26,721 --> 00:03:28,095
-不要 -是谁
- No. ?- Who's there?

104
00:03:29,860 --> 00:03:31,700
我亲爱的家人们
My darling family.

105
00:03:32,020 --> 00:03:33,012
你们来了
You came.

106
00:03:33,012 --> 00:03:34,300
她的嘴哪里不对劲
Something's wrong with her mouth.

107
00:03:34,300 --> 00:03:35,140
她在笑
She's smiling.

108
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:38,680
米奇尔 你变得真英俊
Mitchell, you've gotten so handsome.

109
00:03:38,960 --> 00:03:41,220
你终于找到一个好女人了吗
Have you finally met a good woman?

110
00:03:41,620 --> 00:03:42,168
不好意思 什么
I'm sorry. What?

111
00:03:42,168 --> 00:03:44,980
你在逗我玩对吗 贝奇 你知道...
You're messing with me, right, Becky? You know that --

112
00:03:44,980 --> 00:03:46,560
大伙 我能和你们聊两句吗
Hey, folks, can I speak with you for a second?

113
00:03:46,940 --> 00:03:49,240
这就像我多年前出柜时一样
This is just like when I came out years ago.

114
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:50,820
她心里清楚得很
She knows what she's doing.

115
00:03:51,160 --> 00:03:52,220
其实 她不清楚
Actually, she doesn't.

116
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:55,140
中风或许造成了贝奇的记忆混乱
The stroke may have scrambled some of Becky's memories.

117
00:03:55,140 --> 00:03:57,260
这么说她不记得我出柜的事了
So she doesn't remember me coming out?

118
00:03:57,440 --> 00:03:57,954
是的
Correct.

119
00:03:57,954 --> 00:04:00,392
她现在以为你是直男
And now presumes you're straight.

120
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:02,180
她这想法我则是无从解释
That part I can't explain.

121
00:04:02,420 --> 00:04:04,160
你有没有试过敲敲她
Have you tried popping her on the noggin?

122
00:04:04,300 --> 00:04:05,920
她不是坏了的点唱机 方茨
She's not a jukebox, Fonzie.

123
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:07,520
再说 那也不管用
And besides, it doesn't work.

124
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:10,580
那只让我叔叔变得更糟了 他再也没醒来
It only made my uncle worse. He never woke up.

125
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:12,820
希望她的记忆之后能恢复
Well, hopefully her memory will return.

126
00:04:13,300 --> 00:04:15,980
通常都是些小事能刺激回忆
Often, it's the little things that trigger recollection --

127
00:04:16,260 --> 00:04:18,440
一种味道 一首歌 一张照片
a smell, a song, a picture,

128
00:04:18,700 --> 00:04:19,960
甚至光靠家人的陪伴也有可能
even just her family.

129
00:04:20,540 --> 00:04:22,460
谢谢您 非常感谢 医生
Thank you. Thank you so much, doctor.

130
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:25,560
你敲死了你叔叔吗
Did you kill your uncle?

131
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:27,640
她不记得我是同性恋
She doesn't remember I'm gay.

132
00:04:27,900 --> 00:04:30,360
我知道 刚刚医生解释时我一直都在
Yeah, no, I know. I was here for the whole explanation.

133
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:32,120
这意味着我能再跟她出柜一次
This means I get to come out to her again.

134
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:34,138
第一次简直是灾难
It was a disaster the first time.

135
00:04:34,138 --> 00:04:37,080
我下不定决心告诉她
I was-I was so wishy-washy about the whole thing

136
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:39,560
当我终于说出"我想我可能是同性恋"时
that when I finally said, "I-I think I might be gay,"

137
00:04:39,699 --> 00:04:41,170
她说"好恶"
she said, "Ew."

138
00:04:41,170 --> 00:04:44,220
你确定她说的不是"好啊"
Are you sure she didn't mean, "Ooh"?

139
00:04:44,220 --> 00:04:46,400
不 之后她说了许多
No, no. It was followed up by a whole bunch of stuff

140
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:47,840
我让耶稣哭泣的话
about me making Jesus cry.

141
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:50,740
二十年来我一直后悔那一刻
For 20 years, I've regretted that moment,

142
00:04:50,740 --> 00:04:53,440
而今天 我有机会重新好好做
and today, I get the chance to make it right.

143
00:04:53,440 --> 00:04:56,500
或者你可以不刺激那个精神错乱的老女人
Or you could just leave a poor, old demented woman alone

144
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:59,520
不把她中风的事变成以你为中心
and not make her stroke all about you.

145
00:04:59,940 --> 00:05:01,740
我到底为什么跟你说这些事
Why do I even bring you to these things?

146
00:05:03,945 --> 00:05:06,600
贝奇姑姑 项链真漂亮
Well, Aunt Becky, what a necklace.

147
00:05:06,600 --> 00:05:07,800
很漂亮不是吗
Isn't it lovely?

148
00:05:08,140 --> 00:05:10,520
是我在列支敦斯登遇见的一位王子给我的
It was a gift from a prince I met in Liechtenstein.

149
00:05:11,420 --> 00:05:11,840
真的吗
Really?

150
00:05:13,960 --> 00:05:16,120
菲尔 那是我的项链
Phil, that is my necklace.

151
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:18,440
老爸和歌洛莉亚的婚礼时我借给她戴
I lent it to her for Dad and Gloria's wedding,

152
00:05:18,540 --> 00:05:19,640
她从没还给我
and she never gave it back.

153
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:21,000
她说她弄丢了
She said she lost it.

154
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:22,800
克莱尔 她才经历了中风
Claire, the woman just had a stroke.

155
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,220
我毕业时 我妈送了我一条
When I graduated, my mother gave me

156
00:05:25,220 --> 00:05:26,860
有特殊意义的项链
a very special necklace,

157
00:05:26,860 --> 00:05:29,020
我拿去退款了才买的这条项链
which I returned so I could get that necklace.

158
00:05:29,960 --> 00:05:30,700
我要拿回来
I'm getting it back.

159
00:05:31,100 --> 00:05:33,240
-你要去哪 -我要去热汤
- Where are you going? - I'm going to heat up the soup.

160
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:35,180
或许汤味能让她恢复记忆
Maybe the smell will jog her memory.

161
00:05:35,380 --> 00:05:36,900
她遭的罪还不够多吗
Hasn't she suffered enough?

162
00:05:36,960 --> 00:05:39,340
我想这两个小家伙是最让我骄傲的
I guess I'm proudest of these two little guys here.

163
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:42,380
这是空间大师500 这是仙乐都
This is the Spacemaster 500, and this is the Xanadu --

164
00:05:42,658 --> 00:05:45,518
普利切特衣柜的最新成员
newest additions to the Pritchett's Closets family.

165
00:05:45,518 --> 00:05:47,120
普利切特衣柜是什么
What's Pritchett's Closets?

166
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:49,420
这该死的病连最美好的事都要毁了
This damn disease doesn't care what it destroys.

167
00:05:49,780 --> 00:05:51,776
我知道有什么能帮你记起来
I know what would help you remember.

168
00:05:51,776 --> 00:05:55,977
乔和曼尼给你录了"早日康复"视频
Joe and Manny made you a "Get well" video.

169
00:05:57,160 --> 00:05:57,799
你知道吗
You know what?

170
00:05:57,799 --> 00:05:59,440
我把手机忘在车里了
I forgot my cellphone in the car.

171
00:05:59,440 --> 00:06:00,458
我去去就回
I'll be right back.

172
00:06:00,458 --> 00:06:03,109
谢谢你 迪迪
Oh, thank you, Dede.

173
00:06:03,109 --> 00:06:04,520
深呼吸
Breathe.

174
00:06:04,520 --> 00:06:06,440
你舒服吗 我能帮你做些什么
Are you comfortable? Can I help you with anything

175
00:06:06,440 --> 00:06:07,340
不恶心的事吗
that's not disgusting?

176
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:08,420
我很好
I'm fine.

177
00:06:09,020 --> 00:06:10,780
但我在想 今年夏天
But I was wondering if, this summer,

178
00:06:10,780 --> 00:06:12,640
能不能把你的钓鱼木屋借给我
I could borrow your fishing cabin.

179
00:06:13,020 --> 00:06:14,020
我的钓鱼木屋吗
My fishing cabin?

180
00:06:14,520 --> 00:06:17,340
我爸有间钓鱼木屋 他保证过会留给我
My dad had a fishing cabin that he promised would go to me,

181
00:06:17,380 --> 00:06:20,360
不过那个两面三刀的混蛋留给了我妹妹贝奇
but the double-crossing bastard left it to my sister Becky,

182
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:21,926
她也两面三刀
who's also a double-crosser.

183
00:06:21,926 --> 00:06:23,800
现在她的记忆成了浆糊
Now that her memory is Swiss cheese,

184
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:25,460
我可以把我的木屋偷回来
I can steal my cabin back.

185
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:27,340
终于啊 好人胜利了
Finally, the good guy wins.

186
00:06:31,100 --> 00:06:32,060
父亲
Hello, Father.

187
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:33,398
阿尔文 儿子
Arvin, my boy!

188
00:06:33,398 --> 00:06:35,789
让我向你介绍
Uh, allow me to introduce to you...

189
00:06:36,202 --> 00:06:37,271
海莉·邓菲
Haley Dunphy.

190
00:06:37,271 --> 00:06:40,160
马尔科姆·费诺曼 幸会
Malcolm Fennerman. It is my pleasure.

191
00:06:40,160 --> 00:06:40,998
做得好 儿子
Nicely done, son.

192
00:06:40,998 --> 00:06:43,413
看到你找了个小姑娘[小屁股]我真高兴
Glad to see you've got yourself a little lass.

193
00:06:43,900 --> 00:06:44,800
他说的是"小姑娘"
He said "lass."

194
00:06:45,540 --> 00:06:48,140
对了 计划稍微有变
Oh, by the way, slight change in plan.

195
00:06:48,420 --> 00:06:51,280
在最后一刻 你妈决定跟我一起来
at the last minute, your mum decided to join me on the trip.

196
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:52,401
-什么 -是的
- What? ?- Yes.

197
00:06:52,401 --> 00:06:54,640
在布莱顿的那个周末后
I, um, can't go anywhere by myself

198
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:56,400
我不能独自去任何地方了
after that weekend in Brighton.

199
00:06:56,760 --> 00:06:57,800
老妈要来 现在吗
Mum's coming here? Now?

200
00:06:58,100 --> 00:06:59,160
一切还好吗
Is everything okay?

201
00:06:59,260 --> 00:07:00,560
我还有喝一杯的时间吗
Is there time to get a drink?

202
00:07:00,660 --> 00:07:02,400
恐怕没有 战斗人员就位
I'm afraid not. Man your battle stations.

203
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:03,080
你好
Hello.

204
00:07:05,400 --> 00:07:07,780
我是艾丽斯·费诺曼博士
I am Dr. Iris Fennerman.

205
00:07:07,780 --> 00:07:09,064
很高兴终于能见到
So nice to finally meet the woman

206
00:07:09,064 --> 00:07:10,480
这位我儿子如此迷恋
with whom my son is so enamored

207
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:11,940
但我却没有任何认识的姑娘
and yet I know nothing about.

208
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:14,700
我只是一个很普通的美国姑娘
Well, I'm just your average American girl,

209
00:07:14,700 --> 00:07:16,609
但幸好我比普通的美国姑娘轻非常多
although much thinner, thank God.

210
00:07:16,609 --> 00:07:18,720
还有 我在诺普工作
Oh, also I work at NERP.

211
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:19,200
什么诺普
Nerp?

212
00:07:21,500 --> 00:07:23,880
纳米电子研究项目的缩写
Nano Electronics Research Project.

213
00:07:24,480 --> 00:07:25,800
我跟海莉是同事
Haley is a colleague.

214
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:27,486
但这是最高机密任务 不可言
It's very top-secret, though. Hush, hush.

215
00:07:27,486 --> 00:07:29,660
我们刚才估计已经透露太多了
We probably already said too much.

216
00:07:29,660 --> 00:07:31,520
马尔科姆 为什么还没位子
Malcolm, how is it we are not seated yet?

217
00:07:31,540 --> 00:07:33,040
我不想...
Well, I didn't want to --

218
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:34,890
又选错桌子嘛
pi--pick the wrong table again.

219
00:07:34,890 --> 00:07:36,740
别傻了 坐哪我都可以
Oh, don't be silly. I'd be happy anywhere.

220
00:07:36,740 --> 00:07:37,400
什么时候开始的
Since when?

221
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:42,560
"纳米电子" 什么鬼
"Nano Electronics"? What was that?

222
00:07:42,660 --> 00:07:43,820
求你啦 你就配合演出一下
Please, just play along.

223
00:07:43,820 --> 00:07:44,920
你们在后面交头接耳什么呢
What's all that whispering back there?

224
00:07:44,920 --> 00:07:48,326
没什么 妈 就聊科学的事
Uh, nothing, Mum. Just, um, science talk.

225
00:07:50,020 --> 00:07:51,137
我实在待不住了
I had to get away.

226
00:07:51,137 --> 00:07:53,280
普里契特家的人又开始发作了
It's getting way too Pritchett-y in there.

227
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:55,560
为什么来疗养院探望要搞那么复杂呢
Why can't they just let this be a fun nursing-home visit?

228
00:07:55,900 --> 00:07:57,860
对啊 我们都来到里弗赛德了
Exactly. We're in Riverside.

229
00:07:57,880 --> 00:07:59,234
我们应该尽情玩耍啊
We should be tearing it up.

230
00:07:59,234 --> 00:08:01,220
我们去玩那个密室逃脱吧
Hey, let's go to that escape room.

231
00:08:01,220 --> 00:08:02,480
我同意
I am in.

232
00:08:02,880 --> 00:08:04,800
歌洛莉亚 我们要去玩密室逃脱
Hey, Gloria. We're going to the escape room.

233
00:08:04,880 --> 00:08:06,400
-你想一起去吗 -感觉很有趣
- You want to come? - That sounds fun.

234
00:08:06,440 --> 00:08:06,840
歌洛莉亚
Gloria!

235
00:08:07,640 --> 00:08:08,896
杰好像需要我
I think Jay needs me.

236
00:08:08,896 --> 00:08:10,200
他很难过
He's very sad. ?Oh.

237
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:11,340
别给她看那影片了
Forget the videos.

238
00:08:11,420 --> 00:08:13,440
我们得让她想不起任何事
We have to keep her from remembering anything

239
00:08:13,440 --> 00:08:15,380
我才能把我的钓鱼木屋拐回来
so I can nab her fishing cabin!

240
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:17,460
我突然有强烈想逃脱的冲动
I suddenly feel like escaping.

241
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:23,260
真庆幸我们决定去玩
I'm so glad we're doing this.

242
00:08:23,260 --> 00:08:24,220
对啊 我也这么觉得
I know. Me, too.

243
00:08:26,086 --> 00:08:29,219
等等 我们好像走错路了
Oh, well, I don't -- I don't think this is the way.

244
00:08:30,260 --> 00:08:31,360
这是什么地方
What is this place?

245
00:08:31,420 --> 00:08:33,320
不知道啊 我们沿着原路回去吧
I don't know. Let's just go back up.

246
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:35,840
惨了 锁上了
Oh, no. It's locked!

247
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:37,680
打电话叫人来开吧 我没带手机
Okay, call someone. I don't have a cellphone.

248
00:08:37,680 --> 00:08:39,020
我收不到任何信号
Okay, well, I don't have any service.

249
00:08:39,040 --> 00:08:41,040
我手机也没信号 两位 如果我们
I don't either. Guys, if we don't figure out

250
00:08:41,040 --> 00:08:41,919
不快点想出办法离开这里
a way to get out of here soon,

251
00:08:41,919 --> 00:08:44,392
那我们就来不及去玩密室逃脱了
we're never gonna make it to the escape room.

252
00:08:47,565 --> 00:08:50,434
海莉 我知道你的工作是最高机密
Haley, I know your job is top secret,

253
00:08:50,434 --> 00:08:53,465
但我真的对纳米科技十分着迷
but I'm so fascinated by nanotechnology --

254
00:08:53,465 --> 00:08:55,827
就是能自我复制的机器人这类的
self-replicating robots and such.

255
00:08:55,827 --> 00:08:58,290
我很有兴趣想听你对灰蛊的看法
I'd love to hear your insight into grey goo.

256
00:08:58,290 --> 00:08:59,780
这题我能回答
Ooh, I can answer that.

257
00:08:59,780 --> 00:09:00,900
那是我最爱的伏特加[灰雁牌]
It's my favorite vodka.

258
00:09:03,702 --> 00:09:07,922
别再聊我了 我好喜欢你这西装外套啊
Enough about me. Um, I love your blazer.

259
00:09:08,220 --> 00:09:09,680
你有像英国女皇一样养柯基犬吗
Do you have a corgi like the queen?

260
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:11,395
最近伦敦挺疯狂啊 对吧
Crazy times in London. Am I right?

261
00:09:11,395 --> 00:09:14,200
我听说你们的... 伦敦大桥要垮下来
I hear that your, um, bridge is falling down,

262
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:14,600
垮下来[儿歌]
falling down.

263
00:09:15,689 --> 00:09:17,922
海莉很明显是在开玩笑啦
Haley is obviously joking.

264
00:09:18,211 --> 00:09:21,160
这个... 她身上有那种美式幽默
It's that -- It's that Yankee sense of humor, you know.

265
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:21,960
"吃我内裤[屎]吧"
"Eat my shorts."

266
00:09:21,986 --> 00:09:23,877
"鸡儿硬啦"
"Schwing!"

267
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:25,380
你的手臂上面是什么
What is that on your arm?

268
00:09:25,860 --> 00:09:26,820
是我手肘
Oh, it's my elbow.

269
00:09:28,260 --> 00:09:28,957
真有趣
How delightful.

270
00:09:28,957 --> 00:09:30,654
格兰芬多加10分
10 points for Gryffindor.

271
00:09:30,654 --> 00:09:32,600
不是 是那个像贴纸的东西
No, the sticker-y thing.

272
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:33,830
其实这是我公司做的
Oh, it's actually from my work.

273
00:09:33,830 --> 00:09:34,409
它能够把大脑的能量...
It channels the energy of your brain --

274
00:09:36,340 --> 00:09:38,160
工作的事情是机密 还记得吗
Can't talk about that. Remember?

275
00:09:38,444 --> 00:09:40,787
好吧 那来聊阿尔文
Fine. Then let's talk about Arvin.

276
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:43,860
你决定好接受博士后研究员职位了吗
Have you reached a decision on your research fellowship?

277
00:09:46,980 --> 00:09:49,420
我决定不接受了
I have decided not to take it.

278
00:09:49,720 --> 00:09:52,300
为什么 你不想去大型强子对撞机做研究吗
Why not? I mean, you'd be working on the CERN collider --

279
00:09:52,580 --> 00:09:54,340
这可是一生难得的机会
It's the opportunity of a lifetime!

280
00:09:54,460 --> 00:09:56,700
我只是不想浪费6个月的时间
Well, I don't feel like spending six months

281
00:09:56,700 --> 00:09:58,860
待在瑞士的地底
underground in S-Switzerland.

282
00:09:58,860 --> 00:09:59,760
拜托你别告诉我
Oh, please, don't tell me

283
00:09:59,760 --> 00:10:01,140
你因为一个小姑娘而拒绝这机会
you're turning this down because of a girl.

284
00:10:01,280 --> 00:10:02,660
听我说 这跟我一点关系都没有
Listen, I had nothing to do with this.

285
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:04,420
亲爱的 你关系可大了
Oh, darling, you have everything to do with this.

286
00:10:04,540 --> 00:10:05,800
你向来就是遇见漂亮女生
You've always shown bad judgment

287
00:10:05,800 --> 00:10:07,220
你就晕头转向 乱下决定
when it comes to a pretty girl.

288
00:10:07,426 --> 00:10:08,080
-这话有失公允吧 -谢谢夸奖
- That's not fair. - Oh, thank you.

289
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:09,860
但好歹你以前从来没让她们
But at least you've never let one of them

290
00:10:09,860 --> 00:10:11,460
影响到你的事业啊
get in the way of your career.

291
00:10:12,260 --> 00:10:14,020
听我说 我才没有要影响到任何东西
Look, I'm not getting in the way of anything.

292
00:10:14,620 --> 00:10:16,300
阿尔文压根没跟我提过
Arvin never told me about it,

293
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:18,320
就算他提了 我也不会懂
and even if he did, I wouldn't understand.

294
00:10:18,800 --> 00:10:21,540
我工作的诺普是一个女演员开的网站
The NERP I work for is a website run by an actress

295
00:10:21,540 --> 00:10:22,760
她觉得自己懂科学
who thinks she knows science

296
00:10:22,760 --> 00:10:24,361
因为她曾经在007系列电影里
because, once in a James Bond movie,

297
00:10:24,361 --> 00:10:26,876
演过一个核物理学家 梦娜·洛特博士
she played a nuclear physicist, Dr. Mona Lott.

298
00:10:27,260 --> 00:10:28,240
海莉 你要去哪里
Haley! Where are you going?

299
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:30,500
有人邀请我到洗手间当研究员
Oh, I was offered a fellowship to the bathroom,

300
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:31,840
我决定接受这邀请
and I'm accepting it!

301
00:10:41,860 --> 00:10:43,780
你还记得我在我的钓鱼木屋里
Do you remember that security system

302
00:10:43,780 --> 00:10:45,400
安装的安保系统吗
I had installed in my fishing cabin?

303
00:10:45,740 --> 00:10:48,100
我最后一次借你用时给了你密码
I gave you the code the last time I let you use it.

304
00:10:48,120 --> 00:10:49,749
我现在忘了那密码了
I can't seem to recall it.

305
00:10:49,749 --> 00:10:51,500
好吧 我想想
Well, okay. Let me think.

306
00:10:51,500 --> 00:10:53,180
钓鱼木屋 那木屋
The cabin, the cabin.

307
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:55,400
那里风景好美
Oh. So pretty up there.

308
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:57,680
-我有老公吗 -去世了
- Did I have a husband? - ?Dead.

309
00:10:57,800 --> 00:11:01,080
现在专心回忆那个密码
Now focus on the code and nothing else.

310
00:11:01,080 --> 00:11:04,140
看看谁做了你最爱喝的汤啊
Hey, look who made you your favorite soup.

311
00:11:04,260 --> 00:11:07,380
没有什么比熟悉的味道更能勾起记忆了
Nothing like a familiar smell to bring back memories.

312
00:11:07,580 --> 00:11:09,940
-她吃过东西了 -是吗 我好像有点饿呢
- She ate. - I did? But I'm sort of hungry.

313
00:11:10,040 --> 00:11:11,037
常言道 治感冒吃饱
Well, feed a cold,

314
00:11:11,037 --> 00:11:12,400
-治中风得饿 把东西拿走
- starve a stroke. - Get that out of her.

315
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:14,440
你来我爸的婚礼时 我做了这个给你喝
I made this for you when you came to Dad's wedding.

316
00:11:15,260 --> 00:11:17,380
我想起来了 你再婚了
?That's right. You got remarried

317
00:11:17,380 --> 00:11:19,080
你娶了那个波多黎各女人
to that Puerto Rican woman.

318
00:11:19,260 --> 00:11:21,260
你在那婚礼上好美啊
You looked so beautiful at that wedding --

319
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:23,978
你的裙子 你的鞋子 还有戴的珠宝
your dress, your shoes, the jewelry.

320
00:11:23,978 --> 00:11:25,460
你过来 失陪一下
Come here a second. Excuse me.

321
00:11:25,460 --> 00:11:26,560
你到底想干嘛
What the hell are you up to?

322
00:11:26,660 --> 00:11:27,420
她偷走了我的项链
She stole my necklace.

323
00:11:27,420 --> 00:11:29,320
所以你试图控制一个生病的女人
So you try to manipulate a sick woman

324
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:30,720
来得到你个人的利益吗
for your own personal agenda?

325
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:32,060
贝奇姑姑 你好啊
Aunt Becky, hi.

326
00:11:32,340 --> 00:11:34,180
你还记得你来看我冰上舞蹈表演
You remember when you came to see me ice dance,

327
00:11:34,300 --> 00:11:36,246
你说我看起来有点娘炮 我...
you said that I looked like a little sissy, well, I --

328
00:11:36,246 --> 00:11:37,216
爸
Ow, Dad!

329
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:40,821
我真是以你们俩为耻啊
I am ashamed of the both of you.

330
00:11:40,821 --> 00:11:41,980
里面躺着的人是我妹妹
That's my sister in there.

331
00:11:41,980 --> 00:11:43,120
我差点就要失去她了
I almost lost her once.

332
00:11:43,480 --> 00:11:44,640
我不想要再失...
I don't want to have to lose...

333
00:11:45,120 --> 00:11:46,660
-天啊 -爸
- Oh, God. - ?Oh, Dad.

334
00:11:47,300 --> 00:11:48,420
对不起
I'm so sorry.

335
00:11:48,420 --> 00:11:49,837
我们很对不起
Uh, we're so sorry.

336
00:11:50,160 --> 00:11:51,260
你说得对 我们太小心眼了
You're right. We're being petty.

337
00:11:51,780 --> 00:11:53,040
是啊 克莱尔是想拿回项链
Well, Claire's is about a necklace

338
00:11:53,040 --> 00:11:54,762
而我是想真实地活下去 不过我懂...
and mine's about living my truth, but I get --

339
00:11:54,762 --> 00:11:55,840
我懂现在不是适当的时候
I get how this isn't the right time.

340
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:56,598
抱歉我情绪失控了
I'm sorry I snapped.

341
00:11:56,598 --> 00:11:58,124
这真的很难熬
This is just hard, you know?

342
00:11:58,124 --> 00:12:00,260
抱歉 你的妹妹说她想起来
Excuse me. Your sister said she remembers something

343
00:12:00,260 --> 00:12:02,340
有关你的钓鱼小屋安保密码的事情
about the security code to your fishing cabin?

344
00:12:03,358 --> 00:12:05,940
我怎么记得那是她的钓鱼小屋
Well, I -- I thought it was her fishing cabin?

345
00:12:05,940 --> 00:12:07,940
天啊 她现在记成是你的
Oh, my God, and she thinks it's yours,

346
00:12:07,940 --> 00:12:10,000
你不想要她重新想起来
and you don't want her to remember it.

347
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:11,340
对啦对啦 你们说得对
Okay, fine. You're right.

348
00:12:12,060 --> 00:12:13,580
但在你们开始指责我之前
But before you start throwing stones,

349
00:12:14,240 --> 00:12:16,780
或许你们应该扪心自...
maybe look deep into your own...

350
00:12:17,383 --> 00:12:18,136
-什么 爸 -什么 不行
- What? Dad. ?- What? No.

351
00:12:18,136 --> 00:12:19,451
-爸 爸 -开门 开门 别关门啊
- Dad. Dad. - No. No, no, no, no, no, no.

352
00:12:19,960 --> 00:12:22,500
好的 我们不用恐慌的吧
All right. We shouldn't be panicking, right?

353
00:12:22,620 --> 00:12:23,540
不用 当然不需要
No, of course not.

354
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:25,500
肯定有无数种我们可以离开这里的方法
There's got to be a million ways out of here.

355
00:12:25,540 --> 00:12:26,860
那里有保安摄像机
There's a security camera.

356
00:12:27,220 --> 00:12:30,220
别 别啊 是旧的早坏了
Oh, no. No, no. It's old and broke.

357
00:12:30,282 --> 00:12:34,519
来人啊 我们被反锁在这里了
Hey! Hey! We're stuck in here!

358
00:12:34,519 --> 00:12:37,139
歌洛莉亚 你这招五分钟前就没用
Gloria. ?Gloria, that didn't work five minutes ago,

359
00:12:37,160 --> 00:12:39,397
在十分钟前也没管用
and it didn't work 10 minutes ago.

360
00:12:39,760 --> 00:12:41,360
为什么没人听到我们
Why can't they hear me?

361
00:12:41,540 --> 00:12:43,500
这通风管肯定得通到别地方啊
This vent has to go somewhere.

362
00:12:43,740 --> 00:12:46,700
歌洛莉亚·玛丽亚·拉米瑞兹·迪尔加多·普里契特
Gloria Maria Ramirez Delgado Pritchett,

363
00:12:46,760 --> 00:12:48,800
-你就是个天才 -我知道
- you are a genius. - I know.

364
00:12:48,880 --> 00:12:50,400
-推我一把 -不 应该是我
- Give me a boost. - No, it should be me.

365
00:12:50,680 --> 00:12:51,880
行吧 歌洛莉亚 你推小卡吧
Right. Gloria, give Cam a boost.

366
00:12:51,900 --> 00:12:53,960
不是啦 我的意思是我来推你
No, I mean, I should give you a boost.

367
00:12:54,300 --> 00:12:55,055
这样能行
Process works.

368
00:12:55,055 --> 00:12:56,800
我们踩那个箱子不行吗
Why don't we use that trunk?

369
00:12:56,800 --> 00:12:59,180
你看 我们几个能相辅相成
See?! We just make each other better.

370
00:12:59,956 --> 00:13:02,080
好了 椅子 椅子 谁需要普里契特那帮人啊
Right, chair, chair. Who needs Pritchetts?!

371
00:13:02,080 --> 00:13:02,980
我来扶着
I'll steady it.

372
00:13:03,140 --> 00:13:04,140
再次谢谢你
Thank you again.

373
00:13:04,896 --> 00:13:06,860
好了 好了 格栅[很棒]
Okay. Okay, grate.

374
00:13:06,860 --> 00:13:07,600
你才棒呢
You're great.

375
00:13:07,666 --> 00:13:09,171
你是说这个格栅啊
Oh, this grate.

376
00:13:09,171 --> 00:13:11,523
我拿住了 好的
I got it. All right.

377
00:13:12,160 --> 00:13:13,540
学电影《虎胆龙威》那样爬吧
Let's "Die Hard" this puppy.

378
00:13:15,800 --> 00:13:16,680
那是我的肩膀
That's my shoulder.

379
00:13:17,540 --> 00:13:19,040
好了 进去吧
Okay, in we go.

380
00:13:19,118 --> 00:13:21,480
好了 菲尔 爬一段就敲几下
All right, now, Phil, every couple of feet, knock

381
00:13:21,480 --> 00:13:23,060
这样我们知道你到哪里了
so we know where you are.

382
00:13:23,140 --> 00:13:23,640
没问题
Got it.

383
00:13:24,080 --> 00:13:25,840
-怎么样 -两位 我好像看到有开口
- Okay? - Guys, I think I see an opening.

384
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,104
我们有救了
We're saved.

385
00:13:27,104 --> 00:13:29,008
呜呼 太好啦 要命啦
Yippie-ki-yay, mother-- oh, dear God.

386
00:13:29,360 --> 00:13:30,740
菲尔 菲尔 菲尔
Phil? Phil? ?Phil?!

387
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,640
好消息 两位 我看到两个人
Good news, guys. I see two people.

388
00:13:32,691 --> 00:13:34,729
或许我可以... 原来是你们啊
Maybe I can get a -- Oh, it's you.

389
00:13:36,540 --> 00:13:38,140
-你好 -海莉 对不起
- Hello? - Haley, I'm sorry.

390
00:13:38,300 --> 00:13:40,040
你生气跑出餐厅是合理的
You had every right to run out of the restaurant.

391
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:42,040
我也是见过不少极品男友的人
You know, I've put up with a lot from boyfriends --

392
00:13:42,220 --> 00:13:43,940
睡车上 爱打游戏 有老婆
futons, video games, wives.

393
00:13:43,963 --> 00:13:45,902
而你居然觉得我丢你人
But you were ashamed of me.

394
00:13:45,960 --> 00:13:48,210
我妈就是个爱品头论足的势利眼
My mother is a judgmental snob!

395
00:13:48,210 --> 00:13:49,767
我希望她能喜欢你嘛
I-I wanted her to like you.

396
00:13:50,037 --> 00:13:52,086
我知道我... 我知道我完全做错了
I know I just -- I handled it all wrong.

397
00:13:52,560 --> 00:13:53,740
但求你回来吧
But please come back.

398
00:13:53,860 --> 00:13:56,020
不要 你让我觉得自己好差
No! You made me feel bad about myself,

399
00:13:56,020 --> 00:13:58,000
而我应该被人更好地对待
and I deserve better than that, okay?

400
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:59,740
所以你就去瑞士吧
So just go to Switzerland

401
00:13:59,740 --> 00:14:03,437
不就去坐在个大东西 比如瑞士巧克力里
and sit in a big thing of, like, Swiss chocolate

402
00:14:03,437 --> 00:14:05,020
然后唱瑞士山歌吧
and -- and yodel, okay?

403
00:14:05,020 --> 00:14:05,780
我们到此为止吧
We're done.

404
00:14:08,580 --> 00:14:09,740
天啊
Oh, my God.

405
00:14:11,140 --> 00:14:12,260
你还好吧
Are you okay?

406
00:14:12,800 --> 00:14:14,800
为什么你们都有口音啊
Why do you all have accents?

407
00:14:21,040 --> 00:14:22,240
怎么回事
What happened?

408
00:14:22,460 --> 00:14:23,380
你晕过去了
You passed out.

409
00:14:23,460 --> 00:14:24,560
你手臂上的贴纸
Those stickers on your arms

410
00:14:24,560 --> 00:14:26,500
上面满载了各式各样的化学物质
are loaded with all sorts of chemicals.

411
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:28,620
我们打给你的紧急联络人了
We called your emergency contacts.

412
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:29,740
你的男朋友来了
Your boyfriend's here.

413
00:14:30,900 --> 00:14:31,600
还好吗 小美女
Hey, sunshine.

414
00:14:35,564 --> 00:14:39,180
安迪 你... 你从犹他州大老远来了吗
Andy? You -- You came all the way from Utah?

415
00:14:39,180 --> 00:14:41,640
没有啦 我刚好回来上一个自助研讨会
Oh, no. I was in town for a self-help seminar --

416
00:14:41,980 --> 00:14:43,420
"如何在正确的时间出现在正确的地点"
"How To Be In The Right Place at the Right Time."

417
00:14:44,060 --> 00:14:44,871
天啊 还真的有用
Holy cow. It's working.

418
00:14:44,871 --> 00:14:47,380
天啊 我估计你的名字在我手机上
Oh, gosh, I guess your name must still be in my phone

419
00:14:47,380 --> 00:14:48,700
还显示是我紧急联络人
as my emergency contact.

420
00:14:48,940 --> 00:14:51,480
我都是输入我男友的名字免得被爸妈训
I use boyfriends to avoid lectures from my parents.

421
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:53,400
我可不想那天在墨西哥的监狱醒来
I don't want to wake up in a Tijuana prison

422
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:55,780
然后还得听他们说"你被禁足了"
and them be all like, "You're grounded."

423
00:14:56,900 --> 00:14:58,360
我很庆幸我能来这里陪你
I'm just glad I could be here.

424
00:14:58,648 --> 00:15:01,591
安迪 我有件事得告诉你
Andy, um, I have to tell you something.

425
00:15:01,622 --> 00:15:02,820
我也真的真的很抱歉
And I'm really, really sorry,

426
00:15:02,820 --> 00:15:05,200
但我现在有对象了
but I'm seeing someone.

427
00:15:06,440 --> 00:15:07,820
-真的吗 -真的
- Really? - ?Yeah.

428
00:15:09,053 --> 00:15:10,761
赞啦
Yes! Whoo-hoo!

429
00:15:10,989 --> 00:15:12,440
真是谢天谢地啊
Oh, thank goodness.

430
00:15:12,440 --> 00:15:14,800
我也有对象了 我只是不知道怎么开口
Me, too. I just didn't know how to tell you,

431
00:15:14,860 --> 00:15:15,920
尤其是在以为你会死的时候
especially if you were dying.

432
00:15:16,162 --> 00:15:17,700
她是个湖人女孩
Oh. ?She's a laker girl.

433
00:15:17,700 --> 00:15:19,960
她是湖人队的拉拉队员啊 不错啊
Oh, wow. A cheerleader. Nice.

434
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:21,180
不是不是不是
No, no, no, no, no, no, no.

435
00:15:21,180 --> 00:15:23,860
约瑟芬在大盐湖帮人的船清除藤壶
Josephine scrapes barnacles off boats in the Great Salt Lake.

436
00:15:23,860 --> 00:15:25,180
我们称呼她们为湖人女孩
We call them laker girls.

437
00:15:25,260 --> 00:15:27,460
不过她们在犹他州也算是性感象征呢
But they are kind of sex symbols in Utah.

438
00:15:28,280 --> 00:15:30,440
所以是谁有幸得到你啊
So, who is the lucky guy?

439
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:33,540
我跟他的感情现在有点一团乱
Well, it's a bit of a mess right now,

440
00:15:33,540 --> 00:15:37,723
不过他是个教授还是个天体物理学家
but, um, he is a professor and an astrophysicist.

441
00:15:37,723 --> 00:15:39,459
他是个真正的天才
He's a -- a legit genius.

442
00:15:39,794 --> 00:15:42,200
海莉 我尽快赶来了
Haley! I came as soon as I heard.

443
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:43,320
其实这不是真的
Actually, that's not true.

444
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:44,240
我中间去吃了个炸玉米饼
I stopped for tacos.

445
00:15:45,580 --> 00:15:46,660
不是他
Not him.

446
00:15:47,460 --> 00:15:48,499
有人有汤匙吗
Anybody got a spoon?

447
00:15:48,499 --> 00:15:49,985
我们可以学《肖申克的救赎》挖洞逃
We could "Shawshank" this thing.

448
00:15:49,985 --> 00:15:52,354
你学《虎胆龙威》时也没多成功啊
It didn't go so well when you "Die Hard"-ed it.

449
00:15:52,780 --> 00:15:54,040
好吧 我先声明
Okay. Full disclosure.

450
00:15:54,180 --> 00:15:55,880
当我感到没人支持时 我大脑会停工
If I don't feel supported, I tend to shut down.

451
00:15:56,040 --> 00:15:56,400
好的
Okay.

452
00:15:56,502 --> 00:15:58,445
我... 我觉得有点喘不过气
I'm, um -- I'm getting stuffy.

453
00:15:58,801 --> 00:16:00,720
这里是不是越来越闷了
Is -- Is it getting stuffy in here?

454
00:16:00,720 --> 00:16:02,780
加把劲啊 这里肯定有东西
Come on. There's got to be something in this place

455
00:16:02,780 --> 00:16:03,680
能帮助我们出去
that can help us.

456
00:16:03,940 --> 00:16:05,220
快看 有电话
Hey, hey! Whoa, whoa! A phone!

457
00:16:05,660 --> 00:16:06,756
这里面有插口吗
Is there a plug around here?

458
00:16:06,756 --> 00:16:08,200
快来找 这里一定有插口
Somebody -- There's got to be a plug.

459
00:16:08,200 --> 00:16:09,100
我们快来找插口
Everybody look for a plug!

460
00:16:09,180 --> 00:16:10,419
如果没有人来这下面怎么办
What if nobody looks down here?!

461
00:16:10,419 --> 00:16:12,630
我们怎么活下去
You know, how are we gonna survive?

462
00:16:12,630 --> 00:16:14,220
我车上有能量条
I -- I had a protein bar in my car.

463
00:16:14,220 --> 00:16:15,240
我为什么没随身带着呢
I don't know why I didn't bring it in.

464
00:16:15,280 --> 00:16:15,900
肯定有插口
Got to be a plug.

465
00:16:16,080 --> 00:16:17,400
这里没有插口
There is no plug!

466
00:16:17,400 --> 00:16:19,165
能量棒里有花生酱跟20克的蛋白质
It was peanut butter and 20 grams of protein.

467
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:21,320
两位 如果真到了那时候 我说认真的
Guys, if it comes to it, and I mean this --

468
00:16:21,320 --> 00:16:22,960
我希望你们俩吃了我活下去
I want you guys to eat me.

469
00:16:23,400 --> 00:16:26,160
就像多年来那几次电梯故障
As I told you before, in those elevators

470
00:16:26,160 --> 00:16:28,560
或者是堵车时我回答你的答案一样
and in the traffic jam years ago,

471
00:16:28,560 --> 00:16:30,160
我才不会吃掉你
I am not going to eat you.

472
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:32,900
你现在这么说 但我们可能逃不出去
Okay, you say that now, but we may not get out of here,

473
00:16:32,900 --> 00:16:34,900
到时候我们可能就得下艰难的决定了
and we may have to make some hard decisions.

474
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:36,179
看看我们的样子
Look what is happening!

475
00:16:36,179 --> 00:16:38,399
他们完全说中了我们现在的模样
Exactly what they said is going to happen!

476
00:16:38,399 --> 00:16:41,160
你过度亢奋而你在恐慌
You're bouncing off the walls and you're panicking!

477
00:16:41,160 --> 00:16:41,880
而你也在大吼大叫
And you're yelling.

478
00:16:42,060 --> 00:16:42,900
我才没有呢
No, I'm not.

479
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,020
克莱尔或许说对了
Look, Claire may be right.

480
00:16:44,020 --> 00:16:45,399
我现在可能精神涣散
I may be unfocused, but --

481
00:16:45,399 --> 00:16:46,585
但换做是她 她也不会表现多好
but she wouldn't be doing any better.

482
00:16:46,585 --> 00:16:48,976
她肯定会精神过度集中在一些白痴小事
She'd be hyper-focused on something stupid like --

483
00:16:49,312 --> 00:16:51,140
比如..."为什么那些线
like -- like, "Why aren't the wires connected

484
00:16:51,140 --> 00:16:52,480
都没有接到保安摄像头上"
to that security camera?"

485
00:16:52,780 --> 00:16:54,720
对啊 为什么都没接上
Yeah, why aren't they connected?

486
00:16:54,920 --> 00:16:56,320
等等 她说到点子上了
Wait. She's onto something.

487
00:16:57,320 --> 00:16:58,360
那些线是被人剪断的
The wires are cut.

488
00:16:58,740 --> 00:17:01,380
为什么会有人要剪斷位在地下室的
Why would someone cut the wires to a security camera

489
00:17:01,380 --> 00:17:02,520
保安摄像头的线路啊
in a basement room?

490
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:04,460
米奇尔这种时候可能就会想出阴谋论
Well, Mitchell would have some conspiracy theory

491
00:17:04,460 --> 00:17:06,460
觉得这里可能是别人进行非法事务的地方
that this is where the staff does illicit behaviors.

492
00:17:06,760 --> 00:17:08,080
肯定是了
That's what it is.

493
00:17:08,800 --> 00:17:12,420
打从我们一到这里我就一直闻到大麻味
I have been smelling marijuana since I got here!

494
00:17:16,580 --> 00:17:17,629
我来扶着歌洛莉亚
I got Gloria.

495
00:17:17,629 --> 00:17:19,980
天啊 她就像个缉毒局嗅毒犬
My God, she's like a DEA dog.

496
00:17:19,980 --> 00:17:21,000
味道是从...
It's coming from...

497
00:17:24,800 --> 00:17:28,140
这下好了 我们有了大麻 但是没打火机
Great. Now we have marijuana and no lighter

498
00:17:28,140 --> 00:17:30,100
只有这把白痴钥匙
and just this stupid key.

499
00:17:30,420 --> 00:17:31,880
我仿佛能听到杰在说
I can hear Jay saying,

500
00:17:31,972 --> 00:17:35,348
"可能那就是门的钥匙呢 傻子"
"Maybe that key opens the door, dummy."

501
00:17:41,080 --> 00:17:43,320
他们绝对不能知道自己比我们聪明多少
They can never know how much smarter they are than us.

502
00:17:43,440 --> 00:17:43,700
绝对不
Never.

503
00:17:43,804 --> 00:17:45,658
你能想起来的 贝奇
You got this, Becky. ?Mm-hmm.

504
00:17:45,740 --> 00:17:48,360
你走进木屋 你按了按钮
You walk in the cabin, you push those buttons.

505
00:17:48,560 --> 00:17:51,000
按了发出 滴 滴 滴 滴
They go beep, boop, boop, boop.

506
00:17:51,340 --> 00:17:52,240
是哪些数字
What are the numbers?

507
00:17:55,280 --> 00:17:56,460
周
Weeks!

508
00:17:56,460 --> 00:17:58,000
我中风三周了
Since I've had my stroke,

509
00:17:58,020 --> 00:18:00,040
这是你第一次来看我
and this is the first time you come and visit,

510
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:02,740
而你心里只想着那间傻逼木屋
and all you can care about is that stupid cabin.

511
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:03,620
等等 不 什么
Wait. No, what?

512
00:18:03,720 --> 00:18:05,540
我的大脑才没事
My brain is fine!

513
00:18:05,640 --> 00:18:06,300
但是医生说...
But the doctor --

514
00:18:06,480 --> 00:18:07,980
那是隔壁病房的弗莱德
That's Fred from next door.

515
00:18:08,100 --> 00:18:09,820
他曾经在肥皂剧里演过一次医生
He played a doctor on a soap opera once,

516
00:18:09,820 --> 00:18:10,780
就留下了那件白大褂
and he kept the coat.

517
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:12,340
但当时是冰球季后赛嘛
But it was hockey playoffs.

518
00:18:12,660 --> 00:18:14,400
太谢谢你了 谢谢
Thank you so much. Thank you.

519
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:16,080
贝奇姑姑 真的很对不起
Oh, Aunt Becky, I'm so sorry.

520
00:18:16,300 --> 00:18:18,420
我刚才跟列支敦士登的王子通完电话
I just got off the phone with the Prince of Liechtenstein.

521
00:18:18,740 --> 00:18:20,880
他现在有很严重的财务困境
He's having some terrible financial troubles.

522
00:18:21,260 --> 00:18:22,740
他要你把那条项链还给他
He's gonna need the necklace back.

523
00:18:22,820 --> 00:18:24,400
这是为了让国民能温饱
You know, to feed his people.

524
00:18:24,480 --> 00:18:25,460
省省吧 小公主
Save it, princess.

525
00:18:25,580 --> 00:18:26,960
她的记忆根本没出问题
There's nothing wrong with her memory.

526
00:18:27,060 --> 00:18:28,360
她就是在整我们
She was messing with us.

527
00:18:28,540 --> 00:18:29,300
很贱吧
Mean, huh?

528
00:18:29,740 --> 00:18:30,220
太坏了
Horrible.

529
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:31,918
那是我的项链 还给我
That's my necklace. Give it back.

530
00:18:31,918 --> 00:18:33,718
等你把我车子那道
Not until you fix the dent

531
00:18:33,780 --> 00:18:35,820
你高中时留下的坑修好在说
you put in my car in high school...

532
00:18:36,060 --> 00:18:37,420
那坑现在还在呢
which is still there!

533
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:38,740
你还留着那台车啊
You kept the Bonneville?

534
00:18:38,900 --> 00:18:41,183
你的口气听不出有否认是凶手啊
That certainly doesn't sound like a denial.

535
00:18:41,183 --> 00:18:42,572
这条项链我要留下
I'm keeping the necklace. Ugh.

536
00:18:42,640 --> 00:18:44,680
那你也还记得我的事吗
So you also know about me too, then?

537
00:18:44,760 --> 00:18:45,620
你怎么了
What about you?

538
00:18:45,700 --> 00:18:46,620
天啊 这要来了
Oh, God. This is happening.

539
00:18:46,620 --> 00:18:48,480
我... 我... 其实我...
Um, I-I, um -- I -- so I --

540
00:18:48,480 --> 00:18:49,617
有话快说
Spit it out.

541
00:18:49,617 --> 00:18:51,558
我来不是想要拿走你任何东西
Uh, I'm not here to take anything from you.

542
00:18:51,580 --> 00:18:52,840
我来是想要当真实的自己
I'm here to be my true self.

543
00:18:52,840 --> 00:18:54,100
-真是要命了 -而真实的我...
- Oh, for God's sake. - And my true self is --

544
00:18:54,100 --> 00:18:54,500
贝奇姑姑
Aunt Becky!

545
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:56,080
我是个...
I am...

546
00:18:56,080 --> 00:18:57,460
律师
a lawyer.

547
00:18:58,000 --> 00:18:59,000
律师吗
A lawyer?

548
00:19:00,020 --> 00:19:00,460
好恶
Ew.

549
00:19:00,540 --> 00:19:01,580
这下两件事都被她说"好恶"了
Well, that's "Ew" for two.

550
00:19:02,400 --> 00:19:03,240
她情况怎么样了
How is she?

551
00:19:03,340 --> 00:19:04,720
不好 能完全康复
Not good. Full recovery.

552
00:19:06,560 --> 00:19:08,280
迪兰 很抱歉你被通知来
Dylan, I'm sorry you got called.

553
00:19:08,500 --> 00:19:10,300
或许你没从电话里删除掉我
Well, maybe you didn't delete me from your phone

554
00:19:10,300 --> 00:19:12,060
是因为你还没从心里删除掉我
because you didn't delete me from your heart.

555
00:19:12,060 --> 00:19:13,400
或者是我忘了删
Or I just forgot.

556
00:19:13,640 --> 00:19:15,401
随你嘴硬 海莉 我结婚了
Right. I'm married, Haley,

557
00:19:15,401 --> 00:19:17,315
我跟她只爱彼此 你得向前看了
and we're monotonous. You got to move on.

558
00:19:17,380 --> 00:19:18,638
真希望我还在昏迷
Ugh. I wish I was still in my coma.

559
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:20,740
她有男朋友了 不是我
She has a boyfriend. Not me.

560
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:21,500
我有女朋友了
I have a girlfriend.

561
00:19:21,820 --> 00:19:22,617
她是个湖人女孩
She's a laker girl.

562
00:19:22,617 --> 00:19:24,859
藤壶清除员吗 性感啊
Oh, barnacle scraper? Hot.

563
00:19:24,980 --> 00:19:27,960
邓菲小姐 这男人也说是你的男朋友
Miss Dunphy? This man also says he's your boyfriend.

564
00:19:28,660 --> 00:19:29,800
我是哪里没做对啊
What am I doing wrong?

565
00:19:30,300 --> 00:19:32,240
海莉 你没事吧
Haley. Are you okay?

566
00:19:32,300 --> 00:19:33,160
我好担心你
I've been so worried.

567
00:19:35,339 --> 00:19:37,000
谁... 这都是谁
Who's -- Who's this?

568
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:39,280
我是在你之前的男友 而他还在我之前
I'm the guy before you, and he's the guy before me.

569
00:19:40,320 --> 00:19:40,713
你们好
Cheers.

570
00:19:40,713 --> 00:19:41,960
海莉
Um, Haley.

571
00:19:41,960 --> 00:19:43,480
我们得聊聊今天发生的事
We need to talk about what happened.

572
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:45,020
你搞砸了 这就是发生的事
You screwed up. That's what happened.

573
00:19:45,100 --> 00:19:46,500
对对对 永远都是我们错
Right. It's always us.

574
00:19:46,500 --> 00:19:48,460
我们说好了那只大肚猪一起养
We go halfsies on a pot-bellied pig,

575
00:19:48,460 --> 00:19:50,740
结果当它开始口吐白沫以及把你老妈
and suddenly it's all mine when it's frothing at the mouth

576
00:19:50,740 --> 00:19:52,360
逼到洗衣房角落时 就是我的猪了
and corners your mom in the laundry room.

577
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:54,340
他撒谎瞒他爸妈我做的工作
Hey, he lied to his parents about my job

578
00:19:54,340 --> 00:19:55,819
因为我让他觉得丢脸了
because he's ashamed of me.

579
00:19:55,819 --> 00:19:59,180
不不 不是的 我没觉得你让我丢脸
Oh, no, no. No. I'm not ashamed of you.

580
00:19:59,180 --> 00:20:00,260
我只是一下子手足无措
I just panicked.

581
00:20:00,460 --> 00:20:02,700
在你走了之后 我跟我妈坦白了你的事
Look, right after you left, I told Mum the truth about you

582
00:20:02,700 --> 00:20:05,320
说了你的工作 以及如果我想拒绝一个工作
and your job and that if I want to turn down a job

583
00:20:05,320 --> 00:20:06,560
好跟你在一起
to be with you,

584
00:20:07,100 --> 00:20:08,160
那也是我的权利
then that's my right.

585
00:20:08,540 --> 00:20:10,560
无所谓了 我们之间就这样吧
Well, it doesn't matter. This isn't working out anyways.

586
00:20:10,727 --> 00:20:12,740
-又来啦 -真的是
- There it is. - Totally.

587
00:20:12,740 --> 00:20:13,476
他们在说什么
What are they talking about?

588
00:20:13,476 --> 00:20:15,540
他们觉得我是在害怕
Ugh, they think that I'm freaking out

589
00:20:15,540 --> 00:20:17,740
因为你选我而没选好工作
because you chose me over that great job,

590
00:20:17,740 --> 00:20:19,180
这表示你对我感情非常浓烈
which means that you have big feelings for me,

591
00:20:19,200 --> 00:20:21,020
这逼得我也得正视对你的感情
which forces me to look at my feelings for you.

592
00:20:21,260 --> 00:20:21,600
然后呢
And?

593
00:20:23,460 --> 00:20:23,940
然后呢
And?

594
00:20:26,280 --> 00:20:26,760
然后...
And...

595
00:20:26,760 --> 00:20:28,320
我也对你有很浓烈的感情
I have big feelings, too.

596
00:20:28,560 --> 00:20:28,940
你有吗
You do?

597
00:20:29,660 --> 00:20:30,140
当然有啊
Yes.

598
00:20:31,180 --> 00:20:32,260
-说出来吧 -你闭嘴
- Say it. - ?Shut up.

599
00:20:32,420 --> 00:20:33,500
我来说吧
I'll say it.

600
00:20:33,580 --> 00:20:35,480
海莉 我爱你
Haley, I love you.

601
00:20:36,760 --> 00:20:38,940
我也爱你
I love you, too.

602
00:20:41,077 --> 00:20:42,816
我一接到电话就立刻赶来了
I came as soon as I got the call.

603
00:20:44,108 --> 00:20:45,517
她的病情预报是怎么样
What's her forecast?

604
00:20:52,600 --> 00:20:53,800
走啊 走走走
Go, go, go, go, go!

605
00:20:56,520 --> 00:20:58,543
拿到手了吗 我给了她一个道别拥抱
Did you get it? I gave her a hug goodbye,

606
00:20:58,543 --> 00:21:01,004
配合我熟练地手法 在第三次尝试之后...
used my sleight-of-hand, and on the third try --

607
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:04,960
用我的魔术来做这种事感觉好坏啊
I feel so naughty using my magic like that.

608
00:21:04,960 --> 00:21:06,280
我爱死你了 宝贝
I love you, baby.

609
00:21:06,380 --> 00:21:08,940
你前男朋友们警告过我你是这样的女人
Your old boyfriends warned me you were like this.

610
00:21:13,382 --> 00:21:15,046
把项链还我
Give me that necklace.

611
00:21:15,700 --> 00:21:16,793
她追上来啦
She's coming

612
00:21:16,793 --> 00:21:18,300
把项链还我
Give me that necklace.

613
00:21:18,300 --> 00:21:19,180
走走走
Go go go.

614
00:21:19,260 --> 00:21:21,060
我们来试试车吧
Watch what this bad boy can do.
